# Commit and push by default

After finishing a coherent set of changes (feature, fix, or milestone), **commit and push to the current branch** unless the user explicitly says not to (e.g. “don’t push”, “keep it local”, “commit only”).

- Follow the repo’s git safety rules (no force-push to main/master, no amending pushed commits, no secrets).
- Prefer one clear commit per finished unit of work.
- Tell the user the commit hash/message and that it was pushed.
